soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: tell a driver whether the firmware still runs

After a standby to RAM the display MIPS stays parked until userspace
restarts it, and a read of a block the firmware had set up does not
answer then, it stops the bus: on the HY310 the HDMI receiver's first
LINK read after the wake never finished, and the SoC watchdog reset the
box 16 s later (08.10.2026, runs L-B and L-A 2, breadcrumbs in the RTC
general purpose words).

cpu_comm_firmware_up() returns false from the park on and from a
restart's stop until its start, from the two words cpu_comm already
keeps for its own call path. No register is read. The receiver asks it
before it starts or restarts its LINK poll.

Compiled out of tree against the R1 kernel with W=1. Measured with the
receiver change that uses it, see there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,18 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_start(unsigned int timeout_ms)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cpu_comm_firmware_start);
 
+/*
+ * Read without the call mutex: both words change under it, and a caller
+ * that needs the answer to hold keeps its own work out of the sleep and
+ * the restart (the receiver stops its poll in its suspend, and the
+ * restart unbinds it).
+ */
+bool cpu_comm_firmware_up(void)
+{
+	return !READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since) && !READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_fw_down);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cpu_comm_firmware_up);
+
 /* ── Proc filesystem ───────────────────────────────────────── */
 
 static int cpu_comm_proc_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
--- a/include/linux/soc/sunxi/h713-cpu-comm.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/sunxi/h713-cpu-comm.h
@@ -249,6 +249,16 @@ int cpu_comm_firmware_start(unsigned int timeout_ms);
 int cpu_comm_register_firmware_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb);
 int cpu_comm_unregister_firmware_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb);
 
+/*
+ * Whether the firmware that set up the receiver and the picture path still
+ * runs: false from the standby park on and from a restart's stop() until
+ * its start(), true otherwise. The software state, no register is read. A
+ * caller that touches a block the firmware set up (the HDMI receiver's
+ * LINK window) asks this before it reads; after the park the first such
+ * read stops the bus.
+ */
+bool cpu_comm_firmware_up(void);
+
 /*
  * The one owner of the MIPS clock (0x02001600) and resets (0x0200160c),
  * sun50i-h713-mips. While it is registered, cpu_comm asks it whether there
@@ -315,6 +325,11 @@ static inline int cpu_comm_unregister_firmware_notifier(struct notifier_block *n
 	return -ENODEV;
 }
 
+static inline bool cpu_comm_firmware_up(void)
+{
+	return false;
+}
+
 #endif /* CONFIG_HY310_CPU_COMM */
 
 #endif /* __LINUX_SOC_SUNXI_H713_CPU_COMM_H */
